          "evidence_hash": "998bdff043c3a0f165048688fa02b26d1ee5772b000177819f800f090d9bdbd1"
        },
        "worked_solution": "First, we will calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, we will set our result equal to $4.$ \n\nThe equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=k$ and $b=3$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{3}{2(k)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe already know that the axis of symmetry is $x=4,$ so we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2k} & =4 \\\\ -3 & =8k \\\\ k & =-\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "difficulty": "moderate",
        "source_knowledge_point_id": "14837"
      },
      {
        "dom_id": "question-106538",
        "name": "Question 2",
        "problem": "Find the axis of symmetry for the parabola $y=4{x}^{2}-16x+5.$",
        "worked_solution": "The equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute $a=4$ and $b=-16$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{(-16)}{2(4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{8} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the axis of symmetry is $x=2.$",
        "answer_fields_complete": true,
        "result": "Incorrect",
        "html": "<div id=\"question-106538\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">2.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/704#14835\">Finding the Axis of Symmetry of a Parabola</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"106538\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>Find the axis of symmetry for the parabola <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"13\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D466 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-msup><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.363em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-script></mjx-msup><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c36\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c35\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5.</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyEasy\">E</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Fri, Oct 16th @ 3:12 AM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\"