        "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14253321/observations/step-q106538-3b906e94e8fa1e72482d.html",
        "screenshot": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14253321/observations/step-q106538-3b906e94e8fa1e72482d.png",
        "worked_solution": "The equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute $a=4$ and $b=-16$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{(-16)}{2(4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{8} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the axis of symmetry is $x=2.$",
        "can_dont_know": false,
        "can_skip": false,
        "question": {
          "dom_id": "step-q106538",
          "name": "Question 2",
          "problem": "Find the axis of symmetry for the parabola $y=4{x}^{2}-16x+5.$",
          "worked_solution": "The equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute $a=4$ and $b=-16$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{(-16)}{2(4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{8} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the axis of symmetry is $x=2.$",
          "calculator_instructions": "",
